# AATA Exercises — Deferred & Skipped (master index)

This is the running master list of every Judson exercise (Chapters 1–4) that the
`aata/*-exercises.md` transliterations could **not** encode, grouped by the piece
of **machinery** whose absence blocks it. When a piece of theory lands, this file
says which exercises it unlocks. The per-file `**Deferred:** …` notes remain in
context in each exercises file; this file is the index.

Format is plain markdown WITHOUT a `.md` extension so the literate checker never
tries to parse the fenced examples here as real proofs.

Legend: **Deferred** = beyond the current kernel/library (named machinery would
unlock it). **Skipped (brutal computation)** = a specific finite numeric
calculation with no abstract mathematical content (2b4m has no computational
evaluator; the general theorem is already available). **RCA** = a 2b4m-architecture
obstacle; see `aata/EXERCISE-RCA`.

